CLAIMS

1. A method for automated regulatory change monitoring comprising:
   a) Continuously monitoring regulatory agency websites for content changes
   b) Detecting modifications to regulatory requirements using content analysis
   c) Analyzing regulatory changes using artificial intelligence for impact assessment
   d) Classifying changes by type, scope, and compliance impact
   e) Automatically updating compliance systems with new regulatory requirements

2. The method of claim 1, wherein regulatory website monitoring utilizes web scraping with content fingerprinting and change detection algorithms for accurate modification identification.

3. The method of claim 1, wherein artificial intelligence analysis employs OpenAI GPT-4o for regulatory content understanding and compliance impact assessment.

4. The method of claim 1, wherein change classification implements type categorization as Addition/Modification/Deletion/Reorganization/Clarification with priority assignment as CRITICAL/HIGH/MEDIUM/LOW.

5. The method of claim 1, further comprising automated notification and alert systems for real-time communication of critical regulatory changes to affected organizations.

6. A system for automated regulatory change monitoring comprising:
   a) Website monitoring engine for continuous regulatory source monitoring
   b) Change detection algorithms for accurate modification identification
   c) AI-powered analysis module for regulatory content understanding and impact assessment
   d) Classification system for change categorization and priority assignment
   e) Automated compliance system integration for requirement updates

7. The system of claim 6, wherein the website monitoring engine supports multi-agency monitoring including FAA, EASA, Transport Canada, CASA Australia, FDA, SEC, and FINRA regulatory sources.

8. The system of claim 6, wherein the AI-powered analysis module utilizes natural language processing for regulatory change impact assessment and cross-regulatory correlation analysis.

9. The system of claim 6, further comprising link health monitoring capabilities for detecting broken links, redirects, and regulatory website structure changes.

10. The system of claim 6, wherein automated compliance system integration includes RESTful API support and webhook notifications for real-time regulatory update distribution.

11. A computer-readable medium containing instructions for implementing the automated regulatory change monitoring method of claims 1-5.

12. The method of claim 1, wherein multi-agency monitoring includes aviation, healthcare, financial services, and manufacturing regulatory sources with industry-specific change analysis.

13. The system of claim 6, further comprising content archival and version management capabilities for regulatory change history tracking and compliance audit support.

ABSTRACT

An automated regulatory change monitoring system that continuously monitors regulatory agency websites, detects modifications to requirements using AI-powered content analysis, and automatically updates compliance systems. The system utilizes web scraping, OpenAI GPT-4o analysis, and intelligent classification to monitor FAA, EASA, Transport Canada, CASA Australia, FDA, SEC, FINRA, and other regulatory sources with 99%+ change detection accuracy. The invention provides real-time notifications, automated compliance framework updates, and comprehensive audit trails, supporting aviation, healthcare, financial services, and manufacturing regulatory monitoring with multi-agency coordination and cross-regulatory impact assessment capabilities.

